# DramaWay UI

Read `docs/design/system.md` before building a section, and `docs/design/figma-baseline.md` for any measured value. Do not call the Figma MCP for numbers that are already in those files.

The Figma file is a visual direction, not a spec: no auto-layout, no variables, no components, no mobile screens. Deviations from it are deliberate and listed in `system.md` — do not "fix" them back.

## Hard rules

- **No pixel values in `components/sections/*`.** Use tokens or the composition classes. Missing something? Add a class in `@layer components` in `globals.css` — never an arbitrary value like `mt-[137px]`.
- **Decorative circles are backgrounds, not elements.** The Figma dot band is 270 identical circles; `DotBand` draws it with `radial-gradient`.
- **Every section survives empty data.** Sanity fields are optional and galleries vary in length; Figma always shows a fixed count.
- **Headings are uppercase** via `@layer base` on `h1–h4`, except `.hero-title` (sentence case on **every** inner-page H1 hero and the homepage), `.pub-cat-head` (Czytelnia category titles: Alexandria Light magenta), `.history-title` (`/fundacja` timeline: Alexandria SemiBold), `.team-bio-name` (`/fundacja` team: Alexandria, no uppercase), and `.blob-row-label` (`/projekty` archive band: MuseoModerno SemiBold magenta, no uppercase). Do not add `uppercase` on each heading, and do not store ALL CAPS in CMS copy.
- **Editorial copy comes from CMS.** Empty field = omit that text on the page. Do not add frontend fallbacks for titles, leads, CTAs, or summaries. `lib/homepage-copy.ts` and `lib/subpage-copy.ts` hold UI chrome only (filter labels, “więcej”, empty-list messages). Listing heroes read `landingPage` singletons the same way. Do not hardcode new Polish editorial strings in JSX. UI chrome is a quote from the Figma frame, or a row in the copy-exceptions table in `docs/design/system.md`. Do not invent synonyms (e.g. „relacje” for „edycje”). Drupal body/summary is not Figma copy — do not rewrite articles to match the file.
- **Framed photos follow the Sanity hotspot.** A frame that crops (`object-fit: cover`: hero, section photo, gallery tile, team circle, person portrait) must use `Media`. It sets `object-position` from `objectPositionFromHotspot` in `lib/sanity/hotspot.ts`, including a Sanity crop. Do not add a raw `next/image` with `object-cover`, and do not build that URL with only `width` and `fit("max")` — the CDN then skips the hotspot and the browser crops from the centre. Pictures that show the whole file (`object-fit: contain`: article figures, lightbox) may use `urlFor(image)` alone; the builder still applies the crop rectangle, and a hotspot is unused because nothing is cut off.

## What exists

Classes: `.page`, `.split` / `.split-text` / `.split-media` / `.split-reverse`, `.content-split` / `.content-split-solo` / `.content-tile-clamp`, `.hero` / `.hero-title` / `.hero-heading` / `.hero-copy` / `.hero-media` / `.hero-stack`, `.site-header` / `.site-nav-overlay`, `.site-footer` / `.footer-brand` / `.footer-quote`, `.cols-3`, `.stack` / `.stack-item` / `.stack-narrow` / `.stack-wide`, `.measure`, `.gallery-mosaic` / `.gallery-tile` / `.gallery-mosaic-more`, `.team-row` / `.team-photo`, `.values-row` / `.values-item` / `.values-label`, `.history-list` / `.history-item` / `.history-marker` / `.history-title`, `.document-list`, `.team-bios` / `.team-bio` / `.team-bio-name` / `.team-bio-blurb` / `.team-copy`, `.body-figure` / `.body-figure-small` / `-medium` / `-wide` / `-left` / `-center` / `-right` / `-inline` + `.body-image`, `.portable-body`, `.pt-term`, `.pt-indent`, `.pt-roster`, `.pt-columns`, `.pt-cta` / `.pt-cta-1` / `-2` / `-3`, `.pt-embed` / `-poster` / `-play` / `-dot`, `.filter-row-switches`, `.pub-cat`, `.pub-row` / `.pub-mark` / `.pub-mark-photo` / `.pub-mark-ink` / `.pub-row-copy` / `.pub-row-lead`, `.blob-row-label` / `.blob-row-compact` / `.blob-row-excerpt`.

Components: `layout/section.tsx`, `visual/dot-band.tsx`, `visual/palette-row.tsx`, `visual/blob.tsx`, `visual/cta-link.tsx`, `visual/media.tsx`, `visual/image-gallery.tsx` (client mosaic + lightbox). Inner pages: `PageHero` (default split as `/`: at `lg+` the text column sets the height and the still fills it with `ratio="none"` so the Sanity hotspot can crop a fluid frame; below `lg` the still is a circle; `data-split-hero` overlays the header at `lg+` without hiding `.subpage-palette`; `layout="stack"` is text-only — no photo, overlay, or DotBand; empty CMS photo keeps the media slot so column widths do not jump; empty CMS title/lead/CTA omits those elements, and an entirely empty hero is omitted; extra hero copy is `children`, not a `PortableBody` import — listing pages must stay free of the gallery client graph), `BlobRow` (`width`: `page` default / `narrow` / `wide`; `density="compact"` two-up from `lg` with magenta `.blob-row-label`, clamped excerpts, right-column stagger; `BlobStack` is the inner list), `FilterRow` (Czytelnia format CTAs; omit empty drawers; hide the row when fewer than two remain), `PublicationCategoryList` (category sections; each heading toggles its own section; `?kategoria=` on arrival opens that one; the address keeps the param only while exactly one section is open), `CzytelniaStack` (Czytelnia rows only: sand mark, optional cover, file opens the PDF and a page row goes to `/czytelnia/{slug}`), `LeadGallery` (mosaic max 4 + lightbox; no section of its own — the edition page puts it in the same section as the body; no `.cols-3` overflow), `TeamRow` (circle portraits), `/fundacja`: `FundacjaValues` (tangent circles, label inside; below `lg` one row, horizontal scroll, nowrap labels), `TeamBios` (photos plus optional `team.body` Portable Text), `FundacjaHistory` (omit when empty; `history.lead` is Portable Text), `FundacjaDocuments` (omit when empty). Editorial copy for inner heroes comes from CMS (`landingPage`, `aboutPage`, `project.summary`). `/kontakt` and `/fundacja` set `data-no-palette`. Footer: `siteSettings.footer` (left logo+address, right quote).

Tokens: colours `sand` `ink` `green` `green-ink` `magenta` `navy` `brand-1…7`; fonts `font-display` `font-body`; sizes `text-display`/`text-h1` 48, `text-h2` 32 (band labels), `text-h3` 24 (section titles), `text-h4` 20 (card titles), `text-lead` 20 (hero + prose), `text-body` 18, `text-nav` 15 (desktop menu), `text-small` 14; rhythm `py-section`; `--gallery-gap` (mosaic gutter, not section spacing); `--content-narrow` / `--content-wide` / `--values-size` / `--values-size-mobile` / `--history-marker` / `--history-gap` / `--body-image-small` / `--body-image-wide` / `--body-image-max`. Size class ≠ HTML tag: one H1, H2 per section, H3 for news cards.

```tsx
// BAD — hardcoded geometry, raw Figma green, no empty-state
<div style={{ marginLeft: 156 }}>
  <a className="text-[#369125]">poznaj nasze projekty</a>
  <img src={url} width={481} height={823} />
</div>

// GOOD
<Section bleed>
  <div className="split">
    <div className="split-text py-section">
      <h2 className="font-display text-h3 font-black">{title}</h2>
      {summary ? <p className="measure mt-8 text-body">{summary}</p> : null}
      {ctaLabel ? <CtaLink href={ctaHref}>{ctaLabel}</CtaLink> : null}
    </div>
    <Media image={image} alt={alt} variant="bleed" className="split-media" />
  </div>
</Section>
```
